10 REM 10 PRINT -- COOL8 EDITION
20 REM AFTER THE C64 ONE-LINER:
30 REM 10 PRINT CHR$(205.5+RND(1)); : GOTO 10
40 REM
50 REM PETSCII 205 AND 206 REACH THE CELL CORNERS, SO THE
60 REM MAZE JOINS UP. OUR FONT IS CP437 AND ITS / AND \
70 REM HAVE SIDE BEARING -- THEY STOP SHORT, AND THE MAZE
80 REM BREAKS AT EVERY CELL EDGE. THE TEXT FONT IS ROM,
90 REM SO THE FIX IS TILE MODE, WHERE THE PATTERN IS RAM.
100 REM MODE 2 IS 40X30 LIKE MODE 1: CELLS ARE SQUARE.
110 REM ONE TILE SERVES BOTH DIAGONALS -- BIT 6 FLIPS IT.
120 MODE 2
130 FOR I=0 TO 15
140 POKE $FF1E,I:READ R,G:POKE $FF1F,R:POKE $FF1F,G
150 NEXT
160 DATA 0,0,15,255,8,0,10,254
170 DATA 12,76,0,197,0,10,14,231
180 DATA 13,133,6,64,15,119,3,51
190 DATA 7,119,10,246,0,143,11,187
200 REM PATTERNS AT $4000; TILE 1 IS AT $4020.
210 POKE $FF20,0:POKE $FF21,$40
220 POKE $FF26,$20:POKE $FF27,$40:POKE $FF28,1
230 REM SCREEN CODE 77 OUT OF THE C64 CHARACTER ROM,
240 REM PIXEL FOR PIXEL, AT 4BPP: PAPER 6, INK 14. IT IS
250 REM TWO AND THREE PIXELS WIDE, NOT ONE, AND IT MEETS
260 REM BOTH CORNERS -- WHICH IS WHY THE MAZE JOINS UP.
270 REM CODE 78 IS ITS EXACT MIRROR, SO BIT 6 IS ENOUGH.
280 FOR I=1 TO 32:READ D:POKE $FF29,D:NEXT
290 DATA 238,102,102,102,238,230,102,102
300 DATA 110,238,102,102,102,238,230,102
310 DATA 102,110,238,102,102,102,238,230
320 DATA 102,102,110,238,102,102,102,238
330 REM THE SCROLL IS THE HARDWARE'S: NOTHING MOVES IN
340 REM MEMORY. THE MAP IS A RING 32 ROWS TALL WITH 30
350 REM SHOWN, $FF18 IS THE FINE STEP INSIDE A TILE, AND
360 REM THE COARSE STEP IS ONE STRIDE ONTO VID_BASE.
370 S=PEEK($FF14)+PEEK($FF15)*256
380 W=S*32:P=0:B=0:N=0
390 FOR C=0 TO 39
400 A=P+C*2
410 POKE $FF26,A AND 255
420 POKE $FF27,A/256
430 POKE $FF29,1
440 POKE $FF29,RND(2)*64
450 NEXT
460 P=(P+S) AND (W-1):N=N+1
470 IF N<31 THEN GOTO 390
480 FOR F=0 TO 7:POKE $FF18,F:FOR D=0 TO 40:NEXT:NEXT
490 B=(B+S) AND (W-1)
500 POKE $FF12,B AND 255:POKE $FF13,B/256
510 GOTO 390
